I use concurrent data structures like ConcurrentHashMap and atomic classes like AtomicInteger for lock-free operations where possible.

For more complex coordination, I use synchronization or locks such as ReentrantLock, but keep the critical section minimal to reduce contention.

I also design services to be stateless and use immutability to avoid shared state issues.

If needed, I use queues or async processing to decouple workloads and control concurrency.

One important edge case is high contention, where excessive locking can degrade performance.

So overall, I use concurrent utilities, reduce shared state, and design for safe and scalable concurrency.”


