Q: “What is stateless design?”
A: “No request-specific data stored in instance memory.”


20) You need to trace a request across multiple layers. How will you do it? — Ready-to-Speak

“To trace a request across multiple layers, I use correlation IDs combined with distributed tracing.

I generate a unique request ID at the entry point and propagate it across all services through headers.

Then I use distributed tracing tools to capture the full request flow, including latency at each service and dependency.

I also ensure structured logging so all logs include the correlation ID for easy search and debugging.

Additionally, I instrument services to capture spans for each operation to get fine-grained visibility.

One important edge case is missing propagation, where a service fails to pass the correlation ID and breaks trace continuity.

So overall, I ensure end-to-end traceability using correlation IDs, tracing, and structured logging.”


Follow-ups

